  "finalText": "The bar chart is built in the Main composition (1920×1080, 6 s). The critique now scores it 100/100.\n\n- **Title:** \"Revenue by quarter\" top-left, with a \"$M\" unit line below it. Both fade and rise in.\n- **Axis:** a thin grey baseline wipes in from the left first (0.3–0.9 s).\n- **Bars:** Q1 to Q4 grow up from the baseline one after another, 0.15 s apart, with Quart Out easing. The grey bars are neutral and Q4 is blue. Q4 overshoots to 106% and settles.\n- **Values:** 12, 18, 15 fade and rise above each bar as it lands. The 27 uses a spring pop at 1.9 s.\n- **Quarter labels:** Q1–Q4 fade in under the baseline, with Q4 in the accent blue.\n- **Hold:** after the build the Q4 bar drifts slowly to 102% so the last 3 s aren't static.\n\nChoices I made that you didn't specify: the bar values are static text, not a counting number, since I used a fade/rise for the labels. I also left out a \"+80% vs Q3\" callout to keep it clean. I can add either if you want them."
